<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<usx version="3.0">
  <book code="1JN" style="id">1 JOHN</book>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="1JN 1"/>
  <para style="s1">Prologue: Concerning the Word of Life</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1JN 1:1"/>
    We are declaring to you what existed from the very beginning—what we have heard with our own ears, what we have witnessed with our own eyes, what we have gazed upon intently, and what our own hands have physically touched—concerning the Word who gives life.
    <verse eid="1JN 1:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1JN 1:2"/>
    The life appeared, and we have seen and now bear witness and proclaim to you the eternal life, which existed in the Father’s presence and was revealed to us.
    <verse eid="1JN 1:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1JN 1:3"/>
    What we ourselves have seen and heard, we now proclaim to you as well, so that you may share in our fellowship. And truly, our fellowship is with the Father and with His Son Jesus Christ.
    <verse eid="1JN 1:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1JN 1:4"/>
    We are writing these things so that our joy may be completely fulfilled. 
    <verse eid="1JN 1:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Walking in the Light</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1JN 1:5"/>
    Here is the message we have received from Him and now announce to you: God is pure Light, and in Him there exists absolutely no darkness whatsoever.
    <verse eid="1JN 1:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1JN 1:6"/>
    If we claim to have fellowship with Him while continuing to walk in darkness, we are lying and not living according to the truth.
    <verse eid="1JN 1:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1JN 1:7"/>
    But if we walk in the Light just as He exists in the Light, we have genuine fellowship with one another, and the blood of Jesus His Son continuously cleanses us from every sin.
    <verse eid="1JN 1:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1JN 1:8"/>
    If we claim to be without sin, we are deceiving ourselves, and the truth has no place in us.
    <verse eid="1JN 1:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1JN 1:9"/>
    If we acknowledge our sins, He is faithful and just to forgive us our sins and to cleanse us from every form of unrighteousness.
    <verse eid="1JN 1:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1JN 1:10"/>
    If we claim we have never sinned, we make Him out to be a liar, and His word has no place in us.
    <verse eid="1JN 1:10"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="1JN 1"/>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="1JN 2"/>
  <para style="s1">Christ, our Advocate with the Father</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1JN 2:1"/>
    My little children, I am writing these things to you so that you will not sin. Yet if anyone does commit sin, we have One who speaks in our defence before the Father—Jesus Christ, the Righteous One.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1JN 2:2"/>
    He Himself is the propitiation for our sins, and not only for ours but also for the sins of the entire world.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1JN 2:3"/>
    We can be sure that we have come to know Him if we obey His commands.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1JN 2:4"/>
    Anyone who claims, “I have come to know Him,” yet fails to obey His commands is a liar, and the truth is not present in that person.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1JN 2:5"/>
    But whoever obeys His word—in that person the love of God has genuinely reached its full expression. This is how we can be certain we are united with Him:
    <verse eid="1JN 2:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1JN 2:6"/>
    Anyone who claims to remain in Him must conduct himself in the same manner as Jesus conducted Himself.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The New Commandment</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1JN 2:7"/>
    Beloved, I am not writing you a new commandment, but rather an old commandment that you have possessed from the beginning. This old commandment is the message you have already heard.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1JN 2:8"/>
    Yet I am writing to you what is in another sense a new commandment, which proves itself true in Him and in you, because the darkness is fading away and the true Light is already shining.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1JN 2:9"/>
    Anyone who claims to be in the Light yet harbours hatred towards his brother remains in darkness to this very moment.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1JN 2:10"/>
    The person who loves his brother lives in the Light, and there is nothing in him that would cause him to stumble.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1JN 2:11"/>
    But the person who hates his brother exists in darkness and walks in darkness, and he has no idea where he is going because the darkness has blinded his eyes.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1JN 2:12"/>
    I am writing to you, little children, because your sins have been forgiven on account of His name.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1JN 2:13"/>
    I am writing to you, fathers, because you have known the One who has existed from the beginning. I am writing to you, young men, because you have conquered the evil one.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1JN 2:14"/>
    I have written to you, children, because you have known the Father. I have written to you, fathers, because you have known the One who has existed from the beginning. I have written to you, young men, because you are spiritually strong, the word of God lives in you, and you have conquered the evil one.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Do not Love the World</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1JN 2:15"/>
    Do not love the world system or anything belonging to the world. If anyone loves the world, the love of the Father is not present in him.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="1JN 2:16"/>
    For everything that exists in the world—the sinful cravings of our flesh, the greedy desires of our eyes, and the arrogant pride in our possessions—does not come from the Father but originates from the world.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1JN 2:17"/>
    The world and its lustful desires are passing away, but the person who does the will of God lives forever.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Last Hour</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1JN 2:18"/>
    Children, this is the final hour, and just as you have heard that the Antichrist is coming, even now many antichrists have appeared, which confirms for us that this is indeed the last hour.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="1JN 2:19"/>
    They departed from our fellowship, but they never truly belonged to us. For if they had genuinely belonged to us, they would have remained with us. But their departure made it evident that none of them truly belonged to us.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="1JN 2:20"/>
    But you have an anointing from the Holy One, and all of you possess knowledge.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="1JN 2:21"/>
    I have not written to you because you lack knowledge of the truth, but rather because you do possess it, and because no lie originates from the truth.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="1JN 2:22"/>
    Who is the liar if not the one who denies that Jesus is the Christ? This is the Antichrist—the one who denies both the Father and the Son.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="1JN 2:23"/>
    Everyone who denies the Son does not have the Father either; the person who acknowledges the Son has the Father as well.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="1JN 2:24"/>
    As for you, let what you heard from the beginning continue to live in you. If what you heard from the beginning continues to live in you, you will also continue to live in union with the Son and the Father.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:24"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="1JN 2:25"/>
    And this is the promise He Himself gave us—eternal life.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:25"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="1JN 2:26"/>
    I have written these things to you concerning those who are trying to lead you astray.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:26"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="1JN 2:27"/>
    But as for you, the anointing you received from Him continues to live in you, and you have no need for anyone to teach you. Rather, since His anointing instructs you about all things, and since it is genuine and not counterfeit, remain in Him just as it has instructed you.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:27"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Confidence Before God</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="1JN 2:28"/>
    And now, little children, remain in Him, so that when He appears we may have confidence and not shrink back in shame before Him at His coming.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:28"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="1JN 2:29"/>
    If you recognise that He is righteous, you also recognise that everyone who practises righteousness has been born of Him.
    <verse eid="1JN 2:29"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="1JN 2"/>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="1JN 3"/>
  <para style="s1">Called as the Children of God</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1JN 3:1"/>
    Consider what remarkable love the Father has lavished on us, that we should be called the children of God—and that is exactly what we are! The reason the world does not recognise us is that it did not recognise Him.
    <verse eid="1JN 3:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1JN 3:2"/>
    Beloved, we are children of God right now, and what we will become has not yet been fully revealed. We know that when Christ appears, we will be like Him, because we will see Him exactly as He is.
    <verse eid="1JN 3:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1JN 3:3"/>
    Everyone who holds this hope in Him purifies himself, just as Christ is pure.
    <verse eid="1JN 3:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Practice of Sin vs. the Practice of Righteousness</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1JN 3:4"/>
    Everyone who practises sin also practises lawlessness; indeed, sin is lawlessness.
    <verse eid="1JN 3:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1JN 3:5"/>
    You know that Christ appeared in order to take away sins, and in Him there is no sin whatsoever.
    <verse eid="1JN 3:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1JN 3:6"/>
    No one who continues to live in Him practises sin habitually. No one who habitually practises sin has truly seen Him or known Him.
    <verse eid="1JN 3:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1JN 3:7"/>
    Little children, do not let anyone deceive you. The person who practises righteousness is righteous, just as Christ is righteous.
    <verse eid="1JN 3:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1JN 3:8"/>
    The person who habitually practises sin belongs to the devil, because the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. The Son of God appeared for this very purpose: to destroy the works of the devil.
    <verse eid="1JN 3:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1JN 3:9"/>
    No one who has been born of God practises sin habitually, because God’s seed remains in him. He cannot continue in a pattern of sin, because he has been born of God.
    <verse eid="1JN 3:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1JN 3:10"/>
    This is how we can distinguish the children of God from the children of the devil: Anyone who does not practise righteousness does not belong to God, nor does anyone who fails to love his brother.
    <verse eid="1JN 3:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Love of Brotherhood</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1JN 3:11"/>
    For this is the message you have heard from the beginning: We should love one another.
    <verse eid="1JN 3:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1JN 3:12"/>
    We must not be like Cain, who belonged to the evil one and murdered his brother. And why did he murder him? Because his own actions were evil while his brother’s actions were righteous.
    <verse eid="1JN 3:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1JN 3:13"/>
    Do not be surprised, brothers and sisters, if the world hates you.
    <verse eid="1JN 3:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1JN 3:14"/>
    We know we have passed from death to life because we love our fellow believers. Anyone who does not love remains in death.
    <verse eid="1JN 3:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1JN 3:15"/>
    Everyone who hates his brother is a murderer, and you know that no murderer has eternal life remaining in him.
    <verse eid="1JN 3:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Practical Outworking of Love</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="1JN 3:16"/>
    This is how we understand love: Christ laid down His life for our benefit, and we ought to lay down our lives for our brothers and sisters.
    <verse eid="1JN 3:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1JN 3:17"/>
    But if someone possesses material resources and sees his brother in need yet closes his heart against him, how can God’s love remain in that person?
    <verse eid="1JN 3:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1JN 3:18"/>
    Little children, let us not love merely with words or speech, but with actions and in truth.
    <verse eid="1JN 3:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Spirit of Truth and the Spirit of Error</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="1JN 3:19"/>
    This is how we will know that we belong to the truth and will set our hearts at rest in His presence:
    <verse eid="1JN 3:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="1JN 3:20"/>
    Even if our heart condemns us, God is greater than our heart, and He knows everything.
    <verse eid="1JN 3:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="1JN 3:21"/>
    Beloved, if our heart does not condemn us, we have confidence in approaching God.
    <verse eid="1JN 3:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="1JN 3:22"/>
    And we receive from Him whatever we ask, because we obey His commandments and do what pleases Him.
    <verse eid="1JN 3:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="1JN 3:23"/>
    This is His commandment: that we believe in the name of His Son, Jesus Christ, and love one another, just as He commanded us.
    <verse eid="1JN 3:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="1JN 3:24"/>
    Those who obey His commandments live in Him, and He in them. This is how we know that He lives in us: by the Spirit He gave us.
    <verse eid="1JN 3:24"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="1JN 3"/>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="1JN 4"/>
  <para style="s1">The Spirit of God and the Spirit of the Antichrist</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1JN 4:1"/>
    Beloved, do not believe every spirit, but test the spirits to determine whether they come from God, because many false prophets have gone out into the world.
    <verse eid="1JN 4:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1JN 4:2"/>
    This is how you can recognise the Spirit of God: Every spirit that acknowledges that Jesus Christ has come in human flesh is from God,
    <verse eid="1JN 4:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1JN 4:3"/>
    and every spirit that does not acknowledge Jesus is not from God. This is the spirit of the antichrist, which you have heard is coming and even now is already in the world.
    <verse eid="1JN 4:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1JN 4:4"/>
    You, little children, belong to God and have overcome them, because the One who is in you is greater than the one who is in the world.
    <verse eid="1JN 4:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1JN 4:5"/>
    They belong to the world and therefore speak from the world’s perspective, and the world listens to them.
    <verse eid="1JN 4:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1JN 4:6"/>
    We belong to God, and whoever knows God listens to us; whoever does not belong to God does not listen to us. This is how we recognise the Spirit of truth and the spirit of falsehood.
    <verse eid="1JN 4:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Supremacy of God’s Love</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1JN 4:7"/>
    Beloved, let us love one another, because love comes from God. Everyone who loves has been born of God and knows God.
    <verse eid="1JN 4:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1JN 4:8"/>
    Whoever does not love does not know God, because God is love.
    <verse eid="1JN 4:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1JN 4:9"/>
    This is how the love of God was revealed among us: God sent His only Son into the world so that we might live through Him.
    <verse eid="1JN 4:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1JN 4:10"/>
    This is what love is: not that we loved God, but that He loved us and sent His Son as the propitiation for our sins.
    <verse eid="1JN 4:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1JN 4:11"/>
    Beloved, since God loved us in this way, we also ought to love one another.
    <verse eid="1JN 4:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1JN 4:12"/>
    No one has ever seen God; but if we love one another, God lives in us and His love is brought to full expression in us.
    <verse eid="1JN 4:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1JN 4:13"/>
    This is how we know that we live in Him and He in us: He has given us of His Spirit.
    <verse eid="1JN 4:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1JN 4:14"/>
    And we have seen and testify that the Father has sent His Son to be the Saviour of the world.
    <verse eid="1JN 4:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1JN 4:15"/>
    If anyone acknowledges that Jesus is the Son of God, God lives in him and he in God.
    <verse eid="1JN 4:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="1JN 4:16"/>
    And so we have come to know and to believe the love God has for us. God is love, and whoever lives in love lives in God, and God lives in him.
    <verse eid="1JN 4:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1JN 4:17"/>
    In this way, love is brought to its full expression among us, so that we will have confidence on the day of judgment, because in this world we are like Jesus.
    <verse eid="1JN 4:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1JN 4:18"/>
    There is no fear in love. Instead, perfect love drives out fear, because fear involves punishment. The person who is afraid has not been perfected in love.
    <verse eid="1JN 4:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="1JN 4:19"/>
    We love because He first loved us.
    <verse eid="1JN 4:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="1JN 4:20"/>
    If anyone claims, “I love God,” yet hates his brother, he is a liar. For whoever does not love his brother whom he has seen cannot love God whom he has not seen.
    <verse eid="1JN 4:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="1JN 4:21"/>
    And He has given us this commandment: Whoever loves God must also love his brother.
    <verse eid="1JN 4:21"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="1JN 4"/>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="1JN 5"/>
  <para style="s1">Faith in the Son of God</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1JN 5:1"/>
    Everyone who believes that Jesus is the Christ has been born of God, and everyone who loves the Father loves His child as well.
    <verse eid="1JN 5:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1JN 5:2"/>
    This is how we know that we love the children of God: When we love God and obey His commandments.
    <verse eid="1JN 5:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1JN 5:3"/>
    For this is what it means to love God: to obey His commandments. And His commandments are not burdensome,
    <verse eid="1JN 5:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1JN 5:4"/>
    because everyone born of God overcomes the world. This is the victory that has overcome the world: our faith.
    <verse eid="1JN 5:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1JN 5:5"/>
    Who is it that overcomes the world? Only the person who believes that Jesus is the Son of God.
    <verse eid="1JN 5:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Testimony about Jesus</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1JN 5:6"/>
    This is the One who came by water and blood—Jesus Christ. He did not come by water only, but by water and blood. And it is the Spirit who testifies, because the Spirit is the truth.
    <verse eid="1JN 5:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1JN 5:7"/>
    For there are three that testify:
    <verse eid="1JN 5:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1JN 5:8"/>
    the Spirit, the water, and the blood; and these three are in complete agreement.
    <verse eid="1JN 5:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1JN 5:9"/>
    If we accept human testimony, God’s testimony is greater, because it is the testimony of God that He has given about His Son.
    <verse eid="1JN 5:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1JN 5:10"/>
    Whoever believes in the Son of God has this testimony in his heart. Whoever does not believe God has made Him out to be a liar, because he has not believed the testimony God has given about His Son.
    <verse eid="1JN 5:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1JN 5:11"/>
    And this is the testimony: God has given us eternal life, and this life is in His Son.
    <verse eid="1JN 5:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1JN 5:12"/>
    Whoever has the Son has life; whoever does not have the Son of God does not have life.
    <verse eid="1JN 5:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Assurance of Eternal Life and Prayer</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1JN 5:13"/>
    I write these things to you who believe in the name of the Son of God so that you may know that you have eternal life.
    <verse eid="1JN 5:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1JN 5:14"/>
    This is the confidence we have in approaching God: that if we ask anything according to His will, He hears us.
    <verse eid="1JN 5:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1JN 5:15"/>
    And if we know that He hears us—whatever we ask—we know that we have what we asked of Him.
    <verse eid="1JN 5:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Sin Leading to Death and the Sin Not Leading to Death</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="1JN 5:16"/>
    If anyone sees his brother committing a sin that does not lead to death, he should pray and God will give him life. I am referring to those whose sin does not lead to death. There is a sin that leads to death. I am not saying he should pray about that.
    <verse eid="1JN 5:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1JN 5:17"/>
    All unrighteousness is sin, but there is sin that does not lead to death.
    <verse eid="1JN 5:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1JN 5:18"/>
    We know that anyone born of God does not continue to sin; the One who was born of God keeps him safe, and the evil one cannot touch him.
    <verse eid="1JN 5:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="1JN 5:19"/>
    We know that we are children of God, and that the whole world lies under the control of the evil one.
    <verse eid="1JN 5:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">True God and Eternal Life</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="1JN 5:20"/>
    We know also that the Son of God has come and has given us understanding, so that we may know Him who is true. And we are in Him who is true by being in His Son Jesus Christ. He is the true God and eternal life.
    <verse eid="1JN 5:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="1JN 5:21"/>
    Little children, keep yourselves from idols.
    <verse eid="1JN 5:21"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="1JN 5"/>
</usx>
